      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not stopping or restarting the announcing is only valid in the case where subtypes are not announced, otherwise if there\u0027s a registration with subtype A, and it\u0027s updated to B, the advertiser should stop announcing packets saying that A exists.\n\nSo after adding support for the \"many subtypes don\u0027t get announced\" use-case, I think this method should be limited to updates for that use-case, otherwise support for stopping/restarting announcing should be added.\n\nMaybe add a comment to mention that the current implementation is intended to be used in cases where subtypes don\u0027t get announced, otherwise that should be added ?\n\nFYI in the case where subtypes are announced, I think restarting the announcing could be implemented by having MdnsRecordRepository#updateService return an AnnouncementInfo when the service wasn\u0027t stopping or exiting. Then if it\u0027s non-null call announcer.stop(id), and if that returns true restart announcing with the AnnouncementInfo.",
      "revId": "e2ccc703a8f58e74bbad592a8caafc2b07274a5e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
